This is a remote position.
What You Will Be Doing
The CONGA Configuration and Data Modeling Analyst is responsible for developing and supporting PRODUCT DATA MODELS for use in CONGA CPQ and SALESFORCE CRM systems. The position requires an individual with strong proficiency in product data modeling. Works collaboratively with technical staff and cross functional teams to develop and deploy configuration solutions to business requirements in support of the functional business areas.
Responsibilities:
Gather, analyze, interpret business rules and requirements;
Analyze, understand product specifications and configuration rules;
Perform hands on data modeling by writing configuration rules and logic;
Create, update and support product data models;
Provide production support of CPQ configurator to business users;
Lead technical design, documentation, and development efforts;
Provide guidance and mentoring to team members and assistance with investigating and correcting data modeling and configuration issues;
Work with internal IT staff to address configuration issues and incidents.
What You Bring To The Team (Qualifications)
MUST HAVE EXPERINCE WITH APTTUS / CONGA CPQ ADMINISTRATOR’
BS degree in Math or Computer Science;
3-5 years’ experience as Business Analyst on IT projects;
3-5 years’ development experience and strong proficiency in ‘PRODUCT DATA MODELING’ and logic-driven algorithms – in the APTTUS / CONGA CPQ ADMINISTRATOR’ module;
Strong ability to develop and debug complex logic, algorithms and configuration rules for product data modeling in the APTTUS / CONGA CPQ ‘ADMINISTRATOR module;’
SALES FORCE ADMIN and CONGA CPQ 201-202 Certifications;
Experience with developing and supporting SALESFORCE APEX;
Java, Java Script and SQL skills preferred;
Understanding of guided selling and concepts;
General understanding of CRM and ERP applications;
Basic knowledge of servers, databases, and client-side technology, augmented with solid logical and systems thinking;
Deadline-oriented, disciplined and self-managed;
Strong troubleshooting and problem solving skills;
Effective working with global, multicultural teams;
Excellent work ethic, communication skills, problem solving and customer support.
