About Us
Brookfield Renewable is the flagship listed renewable power company of Brookfield Corporation, a leading global alternative asset manager with over $825 billion of assets under management.
Brookfield Renewable operates one of the world’s largest publicly traded, pure-play renewable power platforms. Our portfolio consists of hydroelectric, wind, utility-scale solar and storage facilities in North America, South America, Europe and Asia, and totals approximately 25,700 megawatts of installed capacity and a development pipeline of approximately 126,000 megawatts of renewable power assets, 12 million metric tonnes per annum ("MMTPA") of carbon capture and storage, 2 million tons of recycled material, 4 million metric million British thermal units of renewable natural gas pipeline, a solar manufacturing facility capable of producing 5,000 MW of panels annually and 1 MMTPA green ammonia facility powered entirely by renewable energy. Leveraging over 120 years of operating experience and industry-leading innovation, we drive value across our extensive clean energy platform and deliver innovative renewable power solutions that accelerate the world towards a low-carbon future. Our value extends well beyond the clean energy we produce to fuel a sustainable, growing economy. From our extensive renewable power fleet, we make positive economic, social, and environmental impacts in the communities where we live and work.
Come Join Us
At Brookfield Renewable, we attract and retain high-performing individuals who are interested in making an impact, driving meaningful change and being part of a fast-paced and collaborative environment. Join a purpose driven winning team, committed to results, in an inclusive and high-performing culture. Together, we contribute to the success of one of the fastest growing and largest publicly traded, pure play renewable power platforms in the world while supporting decarbonization and greater energy sustainability to facilitate the global transition to a net-zero.
About the Role
Reporting to the Vice President, Human Resources, the Analyst, Human Resources supports activities related to Human Resources (“HR”) analytics within the corporate office. The Analyst is involved in various aspects of the Corporate HR function, but will predominately lead quantitative analysis and reporting, and will assist in managing the annual compensation planning and administration process. This role requires excellent analytical skills.
The Analyst, HR works in close collaboration with the VP, HR as well as HR colleagues across the global operations of Brookfield Renewable to gather information, consolidate and analyze data, and produce reports to address business requirements.
More specifically, the Analyst, HR has the following responsibilities:
Key Responsibilities
HR Analytics and Reporting
Work with the Corporate team on global HR reporting requirements to support business needs in areas such as workforce planning, financial analysis, Environmental, Social and Governance (“ESG”), corporate communications, compliance and year-end disclosure;
Collect information, prepare and analyze reports using data from different sources, including the Human Resources Information System, coordinate and consolidate global reports;
Support the annual budget preparation for labour costs and partner with the Finance team to create monthly and quarterly forecasting reports;
Address various information requests from different functions across the organization.
Compensation Management
Participate in compensation initiatives, including completing salary surveys, interpreting data and supporting the design and implementation of compensation structures;
Provide analytical support for the execution and administration of compensation programs;
Support global executive compensation planning across Brookfield Renewable and the annual year end compensation process within the Corporate office;
Administer Brookfield Renewable’s long term incentive plans, including managing the granting process, maintaining records in the system used for LTIP administration and implementing changes as required.
Knowledge and Experience Required
Hold a university degree in Business Administration, Human Resources or in a related field;
Relevant work experience in a Human Resources function, preferably in private sector organizations;
Experience in gathering and analyzing data, and preparing reports to address business information requests;
Experience in supporting compensation programs, including short-term and long-term incentive plans;
Advanced Excel skills required; experience in developing and maintaining complex spreadsheets;
Experience working with Human Resources Information Systems.
Candidate Profile
Ability to work in a dynamic, fast paced environment and to adapt quickly to changing priorities;
Results-oriented and problem solver; ability to “roll up” her/his sleeves and get involved at a detailed level to ensure that appropriate solutions are delivered in a timely way;
Proactive and resourceful; seeks to understand the core of issues and develop solutions to mitigate impact and address long term requirements;
Strong analytical skills with a quantitative mindset;
Ability to work independently to gather and analyze information and data, and present findings in a concise format;
High attention to details and focus on quality of output;
A team player; ability to adapt to different styles and to develop cooperative relationships with employees at all levels in the organization;
Excellent communication skills (oral and written) in English; French is considered an asset.
Working here, you will enjoy:
At Brookfield, your goals are a priority. We start with your strengths and ambitions as an employee and strive to create opportunities to tap into your potential.
We work to recognize you in meaningful, personalized ways including a competitive salary, bonus structure, a defined contribution pension plan along with a health benefits program.
Our spaces are open, dynamic, and collaborative, giving you access to different businesses and teams. For your wellbeing, our building is equipped with a modern gym, bike storage, and healthy snacks and drinks.
We cultivate a culture where we invest in your growth and development.
