Involvement with the preparation of forecasting and business planning process;
Support annual valuation process including in-depth review of models/long-term assumptions and the preparation of management presentations;
Ad-hoc analyses and presentations on financial and operational results, as well as supporting any special projects;
Requirements
Recognized professional accounting designation (CPA, CA preferred);
Minimum three to five (3-5) years of work experience in an accounting function, with a track record of high performance;
Advisory or corporate finance experience at a recognized firm or FP&A at a leading organization would be an asset;
Highly proficient in Excel, including the ability to model and use advanced functions;
Highly proficient in PowerPoint, including the ability to generate capitating presentations;
Strong attention to detail, is a must, with the ability to deliver management-ready materials;
Demonstrated leadership ability and is a team player;
Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills and mentality;
