The
Sales & Distribution Business Analyst
designs, implements and supports business solutions within the internal and external sales teams and the supply chain. He/she ensures that they deliver the expected value to the organization in a perspective of optimization, continuous improvement and innovation. He/she uses his/her advanced knowledge of the SAP Sales & Distribution (SD) module and his/her experience in sales and order management to support the management team in the development and implementation of the business vision.
Assigned Responsibilities
Ensure the stabilization of SAP SD modules by contributing as a leader to the design, documentation, testing, implementation, training and coaching of the order management and supply chain solutions;
Support business process performance management by contributing to the creation of dashboards using business intelligence tools to identify sources of non-performance;
Act as a business expert in the analysis and resolution of problems by proposing concrete, effective solutions adapted to the context, while ensuring that the processes evolve in a compatible and effective manner;
Ensure coordination of efforts with analysts from other business units in the development of solutions, particularly in the definition of requirements, testing phases and analysis of impacts on existing processes;
Develop a business partner relationship with managers in order to influence operational teams in the development and use of best practices;
Demonstrate a high sense of autonomy and prioritization by ensuring close communication with colleagues and manager.
Success Factors
Technical background: Your Bachelor's degree in Business, Supply Chain Management or Administration (or equivalent), combined with your 3 years of experience in process analysis, allows you to understand current supply chain issues in a fast-growing environment;
SAP Expertise: Your mastery and experience with SAP Sales & Distribution (SD) modules helps you to quickly integrate the project team and bring value (knowledge of other modules such as MM/PP/EWM/SCM/FICO are real assets);
Analytical mind: You have a facility to conceive and analyze complex situations and to come up with simple customer service oriented solutions adapted to the business context;
Business partner: You always opt for a collaborative and solution-oriented approach. Your interpersonal skills and your advice following your analyses are highly appreciated since you favour communication and exchanges with your collaborators in the achievement of your objectives;
Rigor and autonomy: You have a concern for work well done and pay attention to fine details in a context of high autonomy;
Dynamic work environment: You are comfortable and resilient in a fast-paced, regularly changing work environment;
Bilingualism: You are bilingual and fluent in both French and English.
